row(35, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'IF WITH A STONE OF THE HAND WHEREBY HE MAY DIE HE STRUCK HIM AND HE DIED, HE IS A MURDERER — THE SIZE CLAUSE, SUPPLIED TWICE OVER BY THE TRANSLATION. {HP(35, 17, (("ואם", "באבן", "יד", "אשר", "ימות", "בה"), "AND IF with A STONE OF THE HAND WHEREBY HE MAY DIE — \'a stone of the hand\' one seat; \'whereby he may die\' at the stone (17), the wood (18) and the unseen stone (23) — never at the iron; the Sifrei 160:3: not liable unless the thing can kill and the place struck can kill (Deuteronomy 19:11 for the place); Exodus 21:18\'s quarrel (\'with a stone or a fist\') the row\'s contrast (computed)"), (("הכהו", "וימת", "רצח", "הוא", "מות", "יומת", "הרצח"), "he struck him and he died; he is a murderer — the murderer shall surely die: the formula\'s second seat (computed)"))} → {AP(35, 17, (("ואם", "באבנא", "דמתנסבא", "בידא"), "and if with a stone THAT IS TAKEN IN THE HAND — the translation opens the hand-word into a clause"), (("דהיא", "כמסת", "די", "ימות", "בה"), "WHICH IS SUFFICIENT that he die by it — the size clause supplied (its word \'sufficient\' at 7:5-8 for the Levites\' service and here at 17, 18, 23); the rows\' \'fills the hand\' the exam\'s"))}')
